  "model": "ADM-8F8-E",
  "models": [
    "ADM-8F8-E"
  ],
  "description": "Data logger with 8 analog inputs, 16 digital inputs, 8 digital outputs and 8 counters: live values, alarm levels, alarm and history browsers, Modbus TCP, RS-232 and RS-485",
  "source": "PROSER ADM-8F8-E Manual de usuario, Rev B1",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "ADM-8F8-E Manual de usuario",
      "url": "https://www.proser.com.ar/assets/downloads/manuales/ManualADM-8F8-E-REV_B1.pdf",
      "note": "Rev B1; section 11, Modbus map",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "192627843080827bae21d89aab57ad7d0dd588a93a4d9cf8383459f0fdd738e3"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The manual lists 108 'float' registers (32 bits) numbered 7001 to 7108, one number per value, and does not say whether each takes two Modbus registers. Here each is placed two registers apart (7001, 7003, 7005 ...), the usual way a 32-bit value is read over Modbus; the manual's number n is at address 7001 + 2 x (n - 7001). This spacing and the word order (big-endian assumed) are not confirmed by the manual: if values look wrong, try consecutive addresses.",
    "Coils are numbered 1000 to 1024 in the manual.",
    "Alarm levels: the manual's descriptions of the _AL_LO and _AL_HI registers of the analog inputs are swapped (LO says 'alto'); the tags are used for the names.",
    "Digital inputs and outputs in the history (DIL, DIH, DO) are bytes with one bit per input or output: 32 means input 6, 34 means inputs 2 and 6.",
    "Alarm status: 0 normal, 1 low, 2 high; alarm type 0 analog input, 1 counter. A changed alarm level takes effect at once but is only kept after coil 1024 is set to 1.",
    "The device speaks Modbus RTU or ASCII on RS-485/RS-232 (up to 38400 bps, 7 or 8 data bits) and Modbus TCP on Ethernet; one slave address applies to all. 9600 8N1 RTU is assumed here.",
    "Written from the manual (Spanish), not tested on a device."
  ],
